Original commit body from 62c8dba:

When a repository has only root-level files and no subdirectories
(or when -x excludes all subdirectory contents), the fallback tree
renderer now shows root-level source and config files instead of
"(empty)".

The fallback tree function `_format_structure_tree_toplevel` now:
- Collects root-level source files matching SOURCE_EXTENSIONS patterns
- Collects root-level config/documentation files (CONFIG/DOCUMENTATION)
- Respects exclude patterns for root-level files
- Respects exclude_tests flag for root-level test files (test_*.py)

Fixes issue where repos like qemu-sgabios showed "(empty)" structure
when run with -x flag, despite having source files at the root level.
